# This prelaunch foundation requires no application credentials or environment variables.
# PORT may be set by your hosting platform for the production server (default: 3000).
# BUILD_STANDALONE=1 selects Next's bundled server during a build; Docker sets it automatically.
# Never add real secrets to this file. No .env file is needed for device-only portfolios.
#
# Optional preparation for a future maintained Google/Apple OAuth integration.
# These server-only settings are syntax-checked; they DO NOT enable sign-in or synchronization.
# Leave them unset until provisioning a provider integration. See docs/authentication.md.
# Never prefix any credential with NEXT_PUBLIC_ or place it in a client component.
# AUTH_ORIGIN=https://your-final-domain.example
# AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<web application client ID ending in .apps.googleusercontent.com>
# AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<Google web application client secret>
# AUTH_APPLE_CLIENT_ID=<Apple Services ID, for example com.example.trade.web>
# AUTH_APPLE_TEAM_ID=<10 uppercase letters/digits>
# AUTH_APPLE_KEY_ID=<10 uppercase letters/digits>
# AUTH_APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=<multiline PKCS8 P-256 private key from Apple's .p8 file>
# Apple private keys require real newlines; do not store literal backslash-n sequences.
